## Authentication & Authorization

### JWT Token Handling

- **Algorithm**: HS256 (HMAC-SHA256)
- **Storage**: HttpOnly cookies — never exposed to browser JavaScript
- **Flags**: `Secure` (HTTPS-only) + `SameSite` (CSRF mitigation)
- **Expiry**: Configurable (default 24 hours)
- **Relevant files**:
  - `web/src/shared/lib/auth.ts` — client-side auth service
  - `web/src/app/api/proxy/[...path]/route.ts` — cookie extraction & forwarding
  - `services/core-engine/src/main.rs` — token validation middleware

### Password Security

- **Algorithm**: Argon2 (memory-hard, ASIC/GPU-resistant)
- **Applied at**: Registration and login verification
- **File**: `services/core-engine/src/handlers/auth.rs`
- Argon2 parameters (memory cost, time cost, parallelism) are tuned for the server hardware and reviewed periodically.

### Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

| Role | Permissions |
|------|------------|
| `user` | Browse, purchase, manage own profile and wallet |
| `developer` | All user permissions + list products, manage payouts |
| `admin` | Full platform access |

- Roles are stored in `profiles.role` (database column)
- Every protected route handler verifies the role extracted from the validated JWT
- Seller-specific endpoints (product management, payouts) require the `developer` role

### GitHub OAuth

- State parameter (cryptographically random) used to prevent CSRF on the OAuth callback
- Authorization code exchanged server-side; client secret never reaches the frontend
- GitHub access tokens are encrypted at rest in `profiles.github_access_token`
- Callback endpoint: `/api/auth/github/callback`

