## Network & Infrastructure Security

### Rate Limiting

Implemented via `actix-governor` middleware with a custom IP extractor:

| Endpoint Category | Limit |
|-------------------|-------|
| Authentication (`/api/auth/*`) | 5 requests / 12 seconds |
| Upload presign (`/api/upload/presign`) | 10 requests / 6 seconds |
| Order verification (`/api/orders/verify`) | 10 requests / 6 seconds |

- IP extracted from `X-Forwarded-For` (set by trusted reverse proxy), with fallback to direct connection IP
- File: `services/core-engine/src/main.rs` (lines 72–91)

### CORS Policy

- Configured via the `CORS_ORIGINS` environment variable
- Default (development): `http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:3001`
- Dynamic origin validation — no wildcard origins permitted in production
- Files: `services/core-engine/src/main.rs`, `web/src/app/api/proxy/[...path]/route.ts`

### Network Isolation (Docker)

```
External Traffic
      │
      ▼
 [frontend network]   ← Next.js, Core Engine, Real-Time
      │
      ▼
 [backend network]    ← PostgreSQL, Redis, SeaweedFS, AI Service, Worker
  (internal: true)    ← NOT reachable from the host network
```

- PostgreSQL and Redis are **never** exposed to the host
- All inter-service traffic stays within the Docker bridge network
- Redis connections require password authentication (`REDIS_URL` with credentials)

### TLS / HTTPS

- TLS termination is handled by an external reverse proxy (NGINX, Caddy, or Cloudflare)
- The application layer expects HTTPS connections in production
- `Secure` cookie flag is set, preventing cookie transmission over plain HTTP
- HSTS is recommended for production — see [Known Limitations](#known-limitations--roadmap)

### SSRF Protection

- API proxy routes enforce an allowlist via the `isAllowedPath()` function
- Allowed prefixes: `products`, `seller/`, `orders`, `reviews`, `notifications`, `wallet`, `upload/`, `profile`, `auth/`, `search`
- All outbound calls to external services (GitHub API, Razorpay) use hardcoded, predefined endpoints — no user-controlled URLs
- File: `web/src/app/api/proxy/[...path]/route.ts`

