## Threat Mitigations

### Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)

| Control | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| Token isolation | JWT in HttpOnly cookie — inaccessible to `document.cookie` |
| Output encoding | React's built-in encoding for all rendered user content |
| Security headers | `X-XSS-Protection`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` |
| Upcoming | Content-Security-Policy (roadmap) |

### Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)

| Control | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| SameSite cookies | Set on the JWT cookie |
| OAuth state | Cryptographically random state parameter per flow |
| Content-Type enforcement | API endpoints reject non-JSON requests |

### SQL Injection

Structurally prevented by SQLx compile-time query checking. No raw string interpolation of user input into SQL queries exists in the codebase.

### Brute Force & Credential Stuffing

| Control | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| Rate limiting | 5 auth requests per 12 seconds per IP |
| Password hashing | Argon2 — computationally expensive per attempt |
| Monitoring | Logging of authentication failures (recommended alert thresholds: >20 failures/min per IP) |

> Account lockout is intentionally not implemented to prevent denial-of-service via lockout attacks on known email addresses.

### Man-in-the-Middle (MITM)

| Control | Mechanism |
|---------|-----------|
| TLS | Enforced at reverse proxy layer |
| Secure cookies | `Secure` flag prevents cookie transmission over HTTP |
| HSTS | Recommended for production (see roadmap) |

### Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)

- API proxy uses an allowlist of permitted path prefixes
- No user-provided URLs are fetched server-side without allowlist validation
- External integrations (GitHub, Razorpay) use statically defined endpoint constants

