## Monitoring & Incident Response

### Health Checks

Every service exposes a `/health` endpoint monitored by Docker Compose:

| Service | Health Check Command |
|---------|---------------------|
| PostgreSQL | `pg_isready -U codehaat -d codehaat` |
| Redis | `redis-cli ping` |
| Core Engine | `GET http://localhost:4001/health` |
| AI Service | `GET http://localhost:4002/health` |
| Real-Time | `GET http://localhost:4004/health` |
| SeaweedFS | `GET http://localhost:8333/` |

### Structured Logging

Security-relevant events are logged by every service:

- Authentication successes and failures
- Authorization rejections
- Rate limiting triggers
- Validation failures
- System errors with correlation IDs

| Service | Logger |
|---------|--------|
| Core Engine (Rust) | `env_logger` |
| Real-Time (Node.js) | `console` + structured JSON |
| AI Service (Python) | Python `logging` module |
| Infra Worker (Go) | `log.Println` / `log.Printf` |

### Recommended Alert Thresholds

| Metric | Threshold | Action |
|--------|-----------|--------|
| Auth failures | > 20/min per IP | Investigate + consider block |
| 5xx error rate | > 1% of requests | Page on-call |
| Rate limit triggers | Sustained > 50/min | Investigate for automated attack |
| Unusual withdrawal amounts | Configurable threshold | Manual review |

