## Known Limitations & Roadmap

### Current Limitations

| # | Limitation | Risk Level | Mitigation |
|---|-----------|------------|------------|
| 1 | No Web Application Firewall (WAF) | Medium | Rely on application-level rate limiting; Cloudflare WAF recommended for production |
| 2 | Missing CSP, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy headers | Medium | Legacy security headers present; modern headers on roadmap |
| 3 | No automated SAST/DAST pipeline | Medium | Manual code review; `cargo audit` and `npm audit` run manually |
| 4 | Stateless JWT — no instant revocation | Low–Medium | Short token TTL mitigates; refresh token + blacklist on roadmap |
| 5 | No MFA on sensitive operations | Medium | Planned: TOTP for withdrawals and account changes |
| 6 | Non-root containers partially implemented | Low | Service containers should run as non-root in production |

### Security Roadmap

- [ ] **Content Security Policy (CSP)** — restrict script, style, and media sources
- [ ] **HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS)** — enforce HTTPS, prevent SSL-stripping
- [ ] **JWT refresh token + blacklist** — enable instant session revocation
- [ ] **Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)** — TOTP for withdrawals and critical account changes
- [ ] **Automated dependency scanning** — CI-integrated `cargo audit`, `npm audit`, `pip-audit`
- [ ] **Container image scanning** — Trivy or Grype in CI pipeline
- [ ] **Structured security event logging** — centralised log aggregation with alerting
- [ ] **Non-root Docker users** — enforce `USER nonroot` in all service Dockerfiles
- [ ] **API versioning** — `/api/v1/` prefix for forward compatibility

